 subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424900 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0950983d-5529-5332-ba75-7636f5397a6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424900 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424901 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424901 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5a731d48-68b1-58c7-b15e-4a787d1f4b44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424901 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424902 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424902 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b098fcf-c1b8-5f75-8b3a-28dc83ab8997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424902 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424903 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424903 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "796d84ed-30ec-5eef-9c9e-3ecd61007abc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424903 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424904 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424904 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9e253f5b-694c-5716-b2be-ec3f736b8398" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424904 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186341855 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
